<svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M2 4h12M2 8h12M2 12h8"></path></svg>
<span>Contents</span>
</button>

<div class="main">
<header class="intro">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="crumbs"><a href="/no-mono-bsr">no-mono-bsr</a> / User guide</nav>
<h1><span class="nowrap">no-mono-bsr</span> user guide</h1>
<p class="lede">no-mono-bsr is the Novation Bass Station Rack running its own v1.5 firmware, so its programs, modes, MIDI and demo are the unit's and the owner's manual applies. This guide covers what the plugin adds. Installing is on the <a href="/download#installing">download page</a>, and the ROM folder, artwork files, the update check and contact are on <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
<ol class="toc">
{toc.map(({ id, title }) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
</ol>
</header>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="start">
<div class="eyebrow">1</div>
<h2>Getting started</h2>

<h3 id="first-start">The first start</h3>
<p>A new instance starts the way a new unit does, switched on with program 00 selected. The 40 factory programs (00-39) are in the firmware, and the 60 user programs (40-99) start as plain tones to build your own sounds from - the manual's "Plain Vanilla" tones.</p>

<h3 id="rom">The ROM</h3>
<p>The firmware is in one 32 KB EPROM, and it isn't included. Put it in the ROM folder (<a href="/support#roms">how the ROM folder works</a>) - MAME's <span class="mono">bassstr</span> zip works as it is. Without it no-mono-bsr makes no sound and the bottom bar says NO ROM.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">SHA1</th><th scope="col">What</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td class="mono">v1.5.bin</td><td>32 KB</td><td class="mono">2c2dc3bee0fabf1e77d02cdf3e53885f2c5b913e</td><td>firmware v1.5</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3 id="artwork">Panel artwork</h3>
<p>The blank places for the two logos, on the front and on the rear, take an SVG or PNG of your own each, named as below, anywhere in the ROM folder (<a href="/support#artwork">how artwork files work</a>). <span class="k">ROMs</span> in the top bar lists them with what each has.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Size</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td class="mono">no-mono-bsr-maker.svg or .png</td><td>The Novation logo, in the display window</td><td>29.0 × 2.8 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">no-mono-bsr-name.svg or .png</td><td>The BassStation Rack logo, lower right</td><td>42.8 × 5.8 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">no-mono-bsr-rear_maker.svg or .png</td><td>The Novation logo on the rear</td><td>88.5 × 8.6 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">no-mono-bsr-rear_name.svg or .png</td><td>The BassStation Rack logo on the rear</td><td>87.7 × 11.9 mm</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The plain names (<span class="mono">maker.svg</span>…) in <span class="path">artwork/bsrack/</span> work too, and win over these.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="panel">
<div class="eyebrow">2</div>
<h2>The panel</h2>
<p>The Rack's front panel, measured from photos. Everything on it works as on the unit except PHONES.</p>
<img src="/media/no-mono-bsr/panel.png" alt="The panel, program 00 on the display" width="2510" height="308" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">

<h3 id="sections">Its sections</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">VOLUME, PORTAMENTO</span> and the WRITE switch, which has to be on ENABLE before you can save a program.</li>
<li><span class="k">DATA ENTRY:</span> the keypad, the display and the mode LEDs, AUDITION/DEMO and MODE SELECT.</li>
<li><span class="k">LFO, OSC 1, OSC 2, OSC 1-2 MOD/SYNC, FILTER and ENVELOPES:</span> the sound, as on the unit.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="unit">What the unit does too</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Soft takeover:</span> a knob only acts once you move it, so a program keeps its own settings until you touch the panel.</li>
<li><span class="k">The v1.5 lock-up:</span> if every knob gets turned within a few seconds, or your DAW moves every parameter at once, v1.5 hangs and ignores notes. The real unit stays like that until you switch it off, and the plugin until you use Reset in State.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="rear">The rear</h3>
<p><span class="k">REAR</span> in the bottom bar turns the unit round. FILTER's EXTERNAL AUDIO INPUT is the plugin's side-chain (<a href="#filter-input">FILTER INPUT</a>), and a cable shows in it while your DAW sends audio there. CV IN, GATE IN, CV OUT, GATE OUT and MIDI THRU are drawn but do nothing.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="bars">
<div class="eyebrow">3</div>
<h2>The bars</h2>

<h3 id="top-bar">The top bar</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">BETA</span> after the name: this version is a beta. About shows the version.</li>
<li><span class="k">ROMs:</span> the ROM folder, the ROM and the <a href="#artwork">artwork</a>, with their full paths, and Show, Change… and Rescan for the folder.</li>
<li><span class="k">State:</span> see <a href="#state">State</a>.</li>
<li><span class="k">About:</span> the version, the ROM folder and artwork in use, the <a href="/support#updates">update check</a>, and links to this guide, the site and the forum. A newer version shows as a button in the bar.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="state">State</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Save to file…</span> saves the instance: the memory (the user programs and settings), the knobs and switches, and where the firmware was.</li>
<li><span class="k">Load from file…</span> loads one.</li>
<li><span class="k">Reset…</span> makes it a new instance, as at the <a href="#first-start">first start</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="bottom-bar">The bottom bar</h3>
<dl class="legend">
<div><dt>REAR</dt><dd>Shows the rear panel (<a href="#rear">The rear</a>).</dd></div>
<div><dt>Status</dt><dd>IDLE while the voice sleeps, the keys you've latched, NO ROM, or on the rear whether EXTERNAL AUDIO INPUT has audio.</dd></div>
<div><dt>?</dt><dd>Shows the list of computer keys over the panel. Any click, ? or Escape closes it.</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="daw">
<div class="eyebrow">4</div>
<h2>MIDI and your DAW</h2>

<h3 id="midi">MIDI</h3>
<p>The plugin's MIDI input is the unit's MIDI IN, and its MIDI output is MIDI OUT, so turning a knob sends its controller as the unit does. A new unit receives and sends on channel 1, and the MIDI RX CH and MIDI TX CH modes change that.</p>

<h3 id="filter-input">FILTER INPUT</h3>
<p>Route a track to the plugin's side-chain and it goes into the filter, as the rear's EXTERNAL AUDIO INPUT does. Turn MIX towards EXT. to hear it, and play a note to open the envelopes, as on the unit. With nothing routed, the jack is empty.</p>

<h3 id="automation">Automation and sessions</h3>
<p>Every knob and switch can be automated. A knob your DAW moves counts as moved, so it takes over from the program at once.</p>
<p>A session saves the instance as <a href="#state">State</a> does. Reopened, it carries on where it was, on the same program with the same edits.</p>
<p>When a note has died away the voice sleeps, and the output is exact zeros. no-mono-bsr reports a 12 s tail.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="keyboard">
<div class="eyebrow">5</div>
<h2>Keyboard and mouse</h2>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Knobs:</span> drag up or down, with Shift for fine steps, or scroll. Double-click for the start position.</li>
<li><span class="k">Switches:</span> click to push the lever a position that way (a two-position one flips), drag it, or scroll.</li>
<li><span class="k">Keys:</span> click. A right-click latches a key down until you click it again.</li>
<li><span class="k">0–9, −, =:</span> the keypad, = being +. The number pad works too. <span class="k">A:</span> AUDITION/DEMO. <span class="k">M:</span> MODE SELECT.</li>
<li><span class="k">?</span> shows the key list, and <span class="k">Escape</span> closes it. Click the panel first. Space goes to your DAW.</li>
<li><span class="k">Window:</span> drag the bottom-right corner.</li>
</ul>
</section>

</div>

</div>
</div>

</Base>

<script>
// The sidebar marks the heading being read and opens its section; the button opens it as a
// drawer on a narrow window. Without this script the sidebar shows every heading.
const nav = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.side')!;
const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.toc-button')!;
const links = [...nav.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a')];
const targets = links.map((a) => document.getElementById(a.hash.slice(1))!);
nav.classList.add('spy');
button.hidden = false;

let current = -1;
function mark() {
  let i = -1;
  targets.forEach((t, j) => { if (t.getBoundingClientRect().top <= 120) i = j; });
  // At the end of the page the last headings can't reach the top: take the one jumped to, if
  // it's in view, or else the last.
  if (innerHeight + scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 2) {
    const jumped = targets.findIndex((t) => '#' + t.id === location.hash);
    i = jumped >= 0 && targets[jumped].getBoundingClientRect().top < innerHeight ? jumped : targets.length - 1;
  }
  if (i === current) return;
  current = i;
  links.forEach((a, j) => {
    a.classList.toggle('on', j === i);
    if (j === i) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location'); else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
  });
  const section = i >= 0 ? links[i].closest('.side > ol > li') : null;
  for (const li of nav.querySelectorAll(':scope > ol > li')) li.classList.toggle('open', li === section);
  reveal();
}

// Keep the marked heading in view when the sidebar is taller than the window.
function reveal() {
  const a = links[current];
  if (!a || nav.scrollHeight <= nav.clientHeight) return;
  if (a.offsetTop < nav.scrollTop || a.offsetTop + a.offsetHeight > nav.scrollTop + nav.clientHeight)
    nav.scrollTop = a.offsetTop - nav.clientHeight / 3;
}

let frame = 0;
const later = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => { frame = 0; mark(); }); };
addEventListener('scroll', later, { passive: true });
addEventListener('resize', later);
addEventListener('hashchange', later);
mark();

function open(on: boolean) {
  nav.classList.toggle('open', on);
  button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(on));
  button.querySelector('span')!.textContent = on ? 'Close' : 'Contents';
  if (on) reveal();
}
button.addEventListener('click', () => open(!nav.classList.contains('open')));
nav.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if ((e.target as Element).closest('a')) open(false); });
document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  if (nav.classList.contains('open') && !nav.contains(e.target as Node) && !button.contains(e.target as Node)) open(false);
});
document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'Escape' && nav.classList.contains('open')) { open(false); button.focus(); }
});
</script>

